  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find the monic polynomial with integer coefficients whose zeroes are $2+\\sqrt{3}$, $2-\\sqrt{3}$, $1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^3-5x^2+5x-1$",
      "worked": "The zeroes give the factors, and the polynomial is monic.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=[x-(2+\\sqrt{3})][x-(2-\\sqrt{3})](x-1)\\\\P(x)&=[(x-2)^2-3](x-1)\\\\P(x)&=(x^2-4x+1)(x-1)\\\\P(x)&=x^3-5x^2+5x-1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
